CRASH-14: return 102 from rule, control and ID calls on a closed project

EN_close frees the network arrays but kept the node, link, control and
rule counts, and 17 toolkit functions had no Openflag check, so their
index checks passed and they used the freed memory. A second EN_close
freed everything again. Each of those functions now returns 102 when no
project is open, and EN_close calls initpointers() after freedata(), so
the counts are zero and the pointers NULL once the project is closed.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-14_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..4b31273 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -360,6 +360,10 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_close(EN_Project p)
     // Free all project data
     freedata(p);
 
+    // Reset the counts and pointers to the freed data, so that a closed
+    // project looks the same as one that was never opened
+    initpointers(p);
+
     // Close output file
     closeoutfile(p);
 
@@ -2207,6 +2211,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setnodeid(EN_Project p, int index, const char *newid)
     Network *net = &p->network;
 
